    "description": "Station in Lower Egypt, located between Thou and Daphnai in the Antonine Itinerary",
    "details": "<p>Several identifications are proposed for this place, mostly based on potential correspondences with the Notitia Dignitatum: on paleographic grounds, Tacasiria (Ala secunda Aegyptiorum) in Parthey and Pinder (Not. Dig. 28.39), or <span>Ta Kastra, i.e.</span> Castra Iudaeorum (Not. Dig <span>28.42</span>) in Worp. Modern locations are proposed by Kees (RE) in the vicinity of mod. Fakûs, or in mod. al-ʿAzzāzī (Löhberg), on grounds of the distances given in the Antonine Itinerary. </p>",
